<title>GERMANY: German inland gas oil keeps climbing, trade thin.</title>
<headline>German inland gas oil keeps climbing, trade thin.</headline>
<text>
<p>(DLR/DM=1.5218)  DM/100 LTRS     DLRS/100 LTRS   LAST DM</p>
<p> HAMBURG	     39.40/39.70     25.89/26.09     38.80/38.90</p>
<p> BREMEN		39.40/39.70     25.89/26.09     38.80/38.90</p>
<p> DUISBURG	    40.00/40.30     26.28/26.48     39.50/39.70</p>
<p> FRANKFURT	   41.10/41.30     27.01/27.14     40.70/40.90</p>
<p> KARLSRUHE	   41.50/41.80     27.27/27.47     41.00/41.10</p>
<p> INGOLSTADT	  42.90/43.20     28.19/28.39     42.40/42.70</p>
<p>German inland gas oil continued to climb on Thursday in line with international markets and strong demand for Rotterdam barges. Demand in the main Rhine stations was weak on Thursday, but stocks remained low. -- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8145</p>
</text>
